Dedent: $(amk.dedent text) strips a block's indent the way compose.mk's banana-block
dedent strips one frame's body, so a foreign program can be indented for reading. The
base is the leading whitespace of the first non-blank line and comes off every line
that starts with it; a blank line becomes empty; a tab-led line under a space base is a
recipe line and passes as it is; a line that does not start with the base is
inconsistent, passes as it is, and draws one warning. The body of a define for an
engine is dedented the same way before its target is entered, and there an
inconsistent line is fatal, since the engine would only misread it. The one routine,
amk_dedent, serves both and any other C caller. $(amk.val.dedent name) is the shortcut
for dedenting a variable's unexpanded value, as the value function reads it.

